No N+1 loops exist — `web/lib/server/conflicts.ts`, `audit.ts`, `entities.ts` are already written as batched/grouped single queries. The actual problem is **missing indexes** to back those queries at scale (runs of thousands of entities, queues of hundreds of conflicts):

```ts
// web/lib/db/schema.ts:214 — conflicts has no index on run_id,
// yet every queue/export read does WHERE conflicts.run_id = $1
export const conflicts = pgTable("conflicts", { ... });

// schema.ts:232 — resolutions has no index on conflict_id,
// yet it's LEFT JOINed on resolutions.conflict_id = conflicts.id everywhere
export const resolutions = pgTable("resolutions", { ... });
```

Fix — add explicit indexes:
```ts
export const conflicts = pgTable("conflicts", {...}, (t) => [
  index("conflicts_run_id_idx").on(t.runId),
]);
export const resolutions = pgTable("resolutions", {...}, (t) => [
  index("resolutions_conflict_id_idx").on(t.conflictId),
]);
```
Same gap on `matches` (no index on `runId`) and `auditLog` (no index on `runId`/`action`, and `listAuditForExport` in `audit.ts:140` is explicitly unpaged). Generate a migration with `npx drizzle-kit generate` once added.

`web/components/conflicts/conflict-focus.tsx:57` and `conflict-dense-table.tsx:65` render up to 100 unmemoized rows. `ConflictQueue`'s `move()` (`conflict-queue.tsx:65`) updates `selectedIndex` on every `j`/`k` keypress, re-rendering all rows even though only 2 actually change class:

```tsx
// conflict-focus.tsx:57 — not memoized
function ListRow({ row, selected }: { row: ConflictRow; selected: boolean }) { ... }

// fix:
const ListRow = React.memo(function ListRow({ row, selected }: Props) { ... });
```
This matters specifically because AGENTS.md's design mandates full keyboard review of 400-row queues — every keystroke currently does ~100x more render work than needed.

`web/components/runs/run-live.tsx:46` — the 2s status poll produces a fresh object reference each tick even when `stats`/`status` haven't changed, forcing `StatGrid` to re-render on every poll:
```tsx
// fix: use select to avoid re-render when values are unchanged
useQuery({
  queryKey: ["run", runId, "status"],
  queryFn: fetchStatus,
  refetchInterval: 2000,
  select: (d) => d, // pair with structural-sharing or a custom equality check
});
```

`web/components/rules/ruleset-editor.tsx:166-179` — O(n²) render due to double `indexOf`:
```tsx
{ordered.map((rule) => {
  const index = rules.indexOf(rule);        // O(n) scan
  return <RuleRow position={ordered.indexOf(rule) + 1} ... />;  // another O(n) scan
})}
```
Fix — pair rules with their index once before sorting:
```tsx
const withIndex = rules.map((rule, index) => ({ rule, index }));
const ordered = [...withIndex].sort(bySpecificity);
{ordered.map(({ rule, index }, position) => (
  <RuleRow key={rule.id} rule={rule} position={position + 1} onChange={(patch) => update(index, patch)} />
))}
```
Low impact today (rulesets are policy tables, tens of rows), but cheap to fix. Engine-side `normalize.py`/`detect.py` are Phase 2 stubs — no redundant fold/severity computation exists to find yet; their docstrings already commit to the correct O(n·k) blocking design.

**Bottom line:** the codebase is disciplined about avoiding N+1s and leaks by construction; the concrete, worth-fixing issues today are the four missing Drizzle indexes (#1) and un-memoized conflict-queue rows (#2). Everything else is either negligible at current scale or not yet built.

